{
  "_comment": "Holding a face with a character LoRA rather than an IPAdapter reference. A LoRA trained on a character is the more reliable of the two — IPAdapter transfers a likeness from one photograph and drifts across poses, while a LoRA has learned the person. Clip skip is set for drawn output because that is what character LoRAs are almost always trained on. Portrait framing comes from the requested dimensions.",
